heat_is_pain	one
perceives	one
capable_pain	one
subject_heat	one
# A1 might be suspected of moving "heat" from a felt sensation (the sense in which P1 calls it a pain) to a quality that matter could carry.
# But C (S17) speaks explicitly of "the greatest heat perceived by sense", and S17 grounds it in Hylas's admission that this heat is a pain. So the text means heat as perceived throughout.
# "Subject of" also means the bearer of a state, the same in A1, C1 and C. So I name no bridge.
